% ============================================================================
% comet-tail-type.query.adj — a worked recall over the comet-tail-type library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what's the difference
% between a comet's two tails?": it states no fact of its own — it only
% `import`s the grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves
% each `?` against the `comet_tail_type` rows and returns the description +
% the table's own source/locator/trust. The second query runs BACKWARD (bind
% the description, recall which tail it names). A comet-related term that is
% not one of these two tails (e.g. `coma`, a different physical part
% entirely) abstains honestly — the engine never invents a tail description.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli comet-tail-type.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "comet-tail-type.adj"

? comet_tail_type(dust_tail, $D)                                    % expect traces_a_broad_gently_curving_path_away_from_the_sun
? comet_tail_type($T, always_points_directly_away_from_the_sun)     % expect ion_tail — reverse recall
? comet_tail_type(coma, $D)                                          % expect abstain — coma is a different physical part, not a tail sub-type
